[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Sir-Starch/eu5-random-new-world/main/docs/images/showcase/rnw_showcase_full.gif[/img]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Sir-Starch/eu5-random-new-world/main/w/en1.png[/img]
[list]
[*][b]Six world types:[/b] Supercontinent, continents, small continents, archipelago, scattered islands, or The Wall, a north–south land barrier or island chain with a mountain spine and optional straits.
[*][b]Natural geography:[/b] Mountain chains with passes and foothills, hooked peninsulas, gulfs and inland seas. Lakes have bays and islands, and rivers flow in and carry on downstream.
[*][b]Room to explore:[/b] A wider Pacific to cross. Island groups stay clear of the new continents, and sea lanes and currents follow the geography.
[*][b]Keep the surprise:[/b] The map is hidden in country selection and mod thumbnails by default. You can still pick a native country from the list, or reveal the map to look around.
[/list]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Sir-Starch/eu5-random-new-world/main/w/en2.png[/img]
[list]
[*][b]Native societies:[/b] Settled countries and decentralized tribes, each with their own cultures, religions and subject relationships. States grow along coasts, terrain and farmland.
[*][b]Extraordinary peoples:[/b] Optionally add great empires, maritime leagues, highland confederations, fractured realms and sacred centers.
[*][b]Campaign content:[/b] Regional stories, formable countries and colonial names give the new world its own flavor.
[/list]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Sir-Starch/eu5-random-new-world/main/w/en3.png[/img]
[list]
[*][b]Tune it:[/b] Adjust resource frequencies, land in native states, peasant share and distance from the Old World. Reroll peoples or resources on the same continent. A World Code keeps your seed and settings.
[*][b]Atlas and queue:[/b] Browse ten map lenses, search places and compare worlds. Queue several worlds, even while another is generating.
[*][b]Languages:[/b] The generator and world text support all eleven official EU5 languages.
[/list]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Sir-Starch/eu5-random-new-world/main/w/en0.png[/img]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Sir-Starch/eu5-random-new-world/main/w/en4.png[/img]
[b]Just want to play?[/b] Subscribe to [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3832180151]RNW: The Wall CWYS[/url], a ready-made world. No generator needed.

To make your own:
[olist]
[*]In EU5’s [b]Mods[/b] menu, find Random New World, click [b]Open folder[/b] and launch [b]Random New World Generator[/b].
[*]Pick a world type and settings, or paste a [b]World Code[/b].
[*]Click [b]Generate[/b] and wait a few minutes.
[*]Enable the new world mod, for example [i]RNW: Small continents 7K3Q[/i], and start a new 1337 campaign.
[/olist]

[quote][b]RAM warning:[/b] Generating needs about 7.5 GB of free RAM. With 16 GB, close EU5 as soon as the generator opens, because the game can eat nearly all your memory even in the main menu. You can also start the generator straight from the mod folder without opening EU5 at all.[/quote]

EU5 can’t generate worlds from inside the game, so the generator is a separate app. It never touches your game installation, and a finished world works without it.

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Sir-Starch/eu5-random-new-world/main/docs/images/proton.png[/img]

The generator window needs WebView2 on Windows or WebKitGTK 4.1 on native Linux. Without them, for example in EU5’s usual Proton prefix, the classic window opens instead. You can also choose it in Settings.

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Sir-Starch/eu5-random-new-world/main/w/en5.png[/img]
[list]
[*][b]Requirements:[/b] EU5 1.4.*. New patches in the 1.4 branch are usually compatible without a generator update. Latest fully verified compatibility: EU5 1.4.7.
[*][b]Windows:[/b] The generator isn’t code-signed. It has run without problems in testing, but if Smart App Control or your antivirus objects, please report it.
[*][b]Saves:[/b] New campaigns only. Keep each save’s original world mod and continue that campaign on the exact EU5 version used to generate its map. A newer game or generator may produce a different world from the same code; updating the generator does not migrate saves.
[*][b]Switching worlds:[/b] Use one RNW world at a time, and restart EU5 when you switch maps.
[/list]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Sir-Starch/eu5-random-new-world/main/w/en6.png[/img]
[list]
[*][b][url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3816832717]Refined Colonization[/url]:[/b] Compatible. [b]Load order: (1) Refined Colonization → (2) generated RNW world mod.[/b]
[*][b]Across the Pillars:[/b] Supported. New World expeditions and treasure fleets use the generated map. The DLC is optional.
[*][b]Multiplayer:[/b] Supported, and tested by the community.
[*][b]Other mods:[/b] Map overhauls and mods that replace the Americas conflict with RNW. Other combinations are untested.
[*][b]Ironman and achievements:[/b] Work under the standard game rules.
[/list]
More in the [url=https://github.com/Sir-Starch/eu5-random-new-world/blob/main/docs/known-limitations.md]known issues[/url]. If you find a bug, report it with your World Code and the saved diagnostics.

